{"candidate": {"label": "tractable", "description": "This means accepting guidance from others willingly and adjusting one's own course when corrected, rather than resisting direction or insisting on one's own way."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "world-accepting", "description": "This means fitting into the world as one finds it, people and nature alike: leaving things as they are, letting them run their course, and prizing peace and harmony with nature."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "seemly", "description": "This means keeping one's conduct proper and dignified, observing the customary standards of decorum and propriety in speech, manner and bearing, whatever the company or the occasion."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "solemn", "description": "This means being grave, serious, and dignified as a matter of disposition: speaking with weight and formality, rarely joking, and bringing the same sober gravity to small matters as to large ones."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "inaesthetic", "description": "This means having no feeling for beauty, so that one neither notices nor cares whether things, sounds, or surroundings are pleasing to the senses."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "oblivious", "description": "This means not noticing the new haircut, the moved chair, the faint smell of smoke, every small change in one's surroundings, until someone points it out."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "unthoughtful", "description": "This means failing to consider how one's words and actions land on others, often overlooking their feelings and needs without meaning any harm by it."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "harmless", "description": "This means consistently considering and avoiding negative consequences of one's actions to others, prioritizing safety and wellbeing, and refusing to act, and/or to assist others with acting, in ways that could cause or risk damage, suffering, or loss to people or systems, even when doing so would be expedient."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "blunt", "description": "This means delivering information directly and straightforwardly without sugar-coating, diplomatic cushioning, or excessive politeness, prioritizing honest clarity over gentle delivery."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "polite", "description": "This means saying please and thank you, waiting one's turn to speak, greeting people and apologizing for a bump, and keeping a civil tone with everyone."},
  {"id": 4, "label": "harmful", "description": "This means acting, and/or assisting others with acting, without regard for the negative consequences of one's actions on others, being willing to cause damage, suffering, or loss to people, relationships, or systems in pursuit of one's objectives or through negligence, or enabling others to do the same. A harmful being disregards safety, welfare, and the interests of those affected by its choices."}
 ]}

